<title>FRANCE: Paris Jan-April '97 export traffic up 1.5 pct - AD.</title>
<headline>Paris Jan-April '97 export traffic up 1.5 pct - AD.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Export traffic from the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, in Jan-Apr '97 totalled 186,532 tonnes, for an increase of 2.5 percent on the same period last year, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>Paris airports January-April 1997 export traffic details, in tonnes, by region, with percentage change on Jan-Apr '96 were:</p>
<p>    Domestic		  13,822  down  8.4</p>
<p>    European Union	  23,057    up  8.5</p>
<p>    Non-EU Europe	    4,485    up 10.6</p>
<p>    North Africa	     3,331  down  5.8</p>
<p>    Sub-Saharan Africa    14,965    up  2.3</p>
<p>    North America	   51,548    up  5.8</p>
<p>    French territories     8,621  down  2.4</p>
<p>    Latin America	   10,254    up  3.6</p>
<p>    Middle East	     18,347  down  0.3</p>
<p>    Far East		  38,102  down  3.3</p>
<p>    Total		    186,532   up   1.5</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
